  "peptideContentBpc157Description": "BPC-157 (Body Protection Compound 157) ist ein synthetisches Peptid aus 15 Aminosäuren, das von einem Protein im Magensaft abgeleitet ist. In Tiermodellen wurde seine Rolle bei der Regeneration von Weichgewebe und Darmschleimhaut untersucht. Klinische Daten beim Menschen sind weiterhin begrenzt.",
  "@peptideContentBpc157Description": {
    "sourceString": "BPC-157 (Body Protection Compound 157) is a 15-amino-acid synthetic peptide derived from a protein found in gastric juice. It has been studied in animal models for its role in soft-tissue and gut-lining repair. Human clinical data remains limited.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for BPC-157."
  },
  "peptideContentBpc157TypicalDose": "250–500 mcg",
  "@peptideContentBpc157TypicalDose": {
    "sourceString": "250–500 mcg",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for BPC-157; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentBpc157HalfLife": "~4 Stunden",
  "@peptideContentBpc157HalfLife": {
    "sourceString": "~4 hours",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for BPC-157."
  },
  "peptideContentBpc157Notes": "In Tierstudien wird BPC-157 häufig gemeinsam mit TB-500 in Forschungsprotokollen zu Sehnen und Bändern erwähnt. Diese Referenz stellt keine Anweisung zur Rekonstitution oder Anwendung dar.",
  "@peptideContentBpc157Notes": {
    "sourceString": "Reconstitute with bacteriostatic water and store refrigerated. Commonly stacked with TB-500 for tendon and ligament recovery protocols in animal studies.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for BPC-157; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentTb500Description": "TB-500 is a synthetic fragment of the naturally occurring protein thymosin beta-4. In animal studies it has been investigated for roles in cellular migration and tissue regeneration. It is widely used off-label by researchers and in veterinary settings.",
